concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12A Witnesses—immunity from liability etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-12a ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the individual who makes the disclosure), subject to section 12B. Meaning of provides assistance  (2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure if the person gives information or produces a document or other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on reasonable grounds to be relevant to:  (a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a disclosure under section 43; or  (b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure investigation; or  (c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS, under subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure. Immunity from civil, criminal or administrative action  (3) The witness is not subject to any civil, criminal or administrative liability (including disciplinary action) because of the assistance provided. Immunity from enforcement of remedies or rights  (4) No contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no contractual or other right may be exercised, against the witness on the basis of the assistance provided." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the individual who makes the disclosure), subject to section 12B. Meaning of provides assistance  (2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure if the person gives information or produces a document or other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on reasonable grounds to be relevant to:  (a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a disclosure under section 43; or  (b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure investigation; or  (c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS, under subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure. Immunity from civil, criminal or administrative action  (3) The witness is not subject to any civil, criminal or administrative liability (including disciplinary action) because of the assistance provided. Immunity from enforcement of remedies or rights  (4) No contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no contractual or other right may be exercised, against the witness on the basis of the assistance provided."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-4 ;
