doc:sec-16 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16 Reinstatement" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person (the applicant), that:  (a) another person (the respondent) has taken, or is taking, a reprisal against the applicant; and  (b) the applicant is or was employed in a particular position with the respondent; and  (c) the reprisal wholly or partly consists, or consisted, of the respondent terminating, or purporting to terminate, the applicant’s employment; the Court may order that the applicant be reinstated in that position or a position at a comparable level." ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17 Multiple orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-17 ;
    values:originalText "The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) may make orders under sections 14, 15 and 16 in respect of the same conduct. 18  Costs only if proceedings instituted vexatiously etc.  (1) In proceedings (including an appeal) in a court in relation to a matter arising under section 14, 15 or 16, the applicant for an order under that section must not be ordered by the court to pay costs incurred by another party to the proceedings, except in accordance with subsection (2).  (2) The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs only if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or   Protection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2 Protections  Division 1  Section 19  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or omission caused the other party to incur the costs." ;
    skos:definition "The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) may make orders under sections 14, 15 and 16 in respect of the same conduct. 18  Costs only if proceedings instituted vexatiously etc.  (1) In proceedings (including an appeal) in a court in relation to a matter arising under section 14, 15 or 16, the applicant for an order under that section must not be ordered by the court to pay costs incurred by another party to the proceedings, except in accordance with subsection (2).  (2) The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs only if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or   Protection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2 Protections  Division 1  Section 19  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or omission caused the other party to incur the costs."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5daf9df5d801d6e8ae79032ba68f7489f00fd1db250a5c14f097ec666d846a26" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf> ;
