concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44A(3) Allocation of disclosure—decision not to allocate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44a-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after making the decision not to allocate the disclosure, the authorised officer of the agency must:  (a) if reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser of:  (i) the decision not to allocate the disclosure, and the reasons for the decision; and  (ii) if the authorised officer has taken action, or proposes to take action, under subsection (2)—the details of the action taken or proposed; and" ;
    skos:definition "(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after making the decision not to allocate the disclosure, the authorised officer of the agency must:  (a) if reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser of:  (i) the decision not to allocate the disclosure, and the reasons for the decision; and  (ii) if the authorised officer has taken action, or proposes to take action, under subsection (2)—the details of the action taken or proposed; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6e04e991166818a998ad31bbc8e19660ce08c07090cbc1fa5371cc385a119038" ;
    values:partOf concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a ;
    cof:pageNumber "63"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorised officer must give written notice to discloser after decision not to allocate disclosure." ;
    dc:description "written notice with reasons and details of action taken or proposed" ;
