    values:originalText "(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after making the decision not to allocate the disclosure, the authorised officer of the agency must:  (a) if reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser of:  (i) the decision not to allocate the disclosure, and the reasons for the decision; and  (ii) if the authorised officer has taken action, or proposes to take action, under subsection (2)—the details of the action taken or proposed; and" ;
