doc:sec-49-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "49(1) Investigative agency using separate investigative powers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Despite section 47, if the agency is an investigative agency that has a separate investigative power in relation to the disclosure, the principal officer of the agency may decide:  (a) to investigate the disclosure under that separate investigative power; and  (b) not to investigate the disclosure, or (if the investigation has started) not to investigate the disclosure further, under this Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-49-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49(2) Investigative agency using separate investigative powers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A separate investigative power, in relation to the disclosure, is a power that an investigative agency has, otherwise than under this Act, to investigate the disclosure. Note 1: Under the Ombudsman Act 1976, the Ombudsman has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the Ombudsman. Note 2: Under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986, the IGIS has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the IGIS." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A separate investigative power, in relation to the disclosure, is a power that an investigative agency has, otherwise than under this Act, to investigate the disclosure. Note 1: Under the Ombudsman Act 1976, the Ombudsman has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the Ombudsman. Note 2: Under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986, the IGIS has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the IGIS."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3b31a8f0e9417d90ff31c5a821d2c5690938d2d0d1615e687a4b5bba9ab059b9" ;
    values:partOf concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-49 ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Separate investigative power for disclosure investigation" ;
