doc:sec-49-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "49(2) Investigative agency using separate investigative powers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A separate investigative power, in relation to the disclosure, is a power that an investigative agency has, otherwise than under this Act, to investigate the disclosure. Note 1: Under the Ombudsman Act 1976, the Ombudsman has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the Ombudsman. Note 2: Under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986, the IGIS has power to investigate a disclosure allocated to the IGIS." ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-49-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49(3) Investigative agency using separate investigative powers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) On completing its investigation of the disclosure under its separate investigative power, the investigative agency must inform:  (a) the principal officers of each of the agencies to which any of the conduct disclosed relates; and  (b) the discloser; that the investigation is complete." ;
    skos:definition "(3) On completing its investigation of the disclosure under its separate investigative power, the investigative agency must inform:  (a) the principal officers of each of the agencies to which any of the conduct disclosed relates; and  (b) the discloser; that the investigation is complete."@en ;
