concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50-ss-4a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50(4A) Notification to discloser"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50-ss-4a ;
    values:originalText "(4A) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser if the principal officer investigates, or further investigates, a disclosure that is no longer subject to a stop action direction under the NACC Act." ;
    skos:definition "(4A) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser if the principal officer investigates, or further investigates, a disclosure that is no longer subject to a stop action direction under the NACC Act."@en ;
