concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50AA Decision not to investigate—referral for investigation under"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50aa ;
    values:originalText "another law or power Scope  (1) This section applies if the principal officer of the agency:  (a) decides under section 48 not to investigate the disclosure, or not to investigate the disclosure further; and  (b) does not decide to investigate the disclosure under a separate investigative power (as mentioned in section 49); and  (c) is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the conduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under another law or power (other than a separate investigative power). Referral of conduct  (2) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct disclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the other law or power." ;
    skos:definition "another law or power Scope  (1) This section applies if the principal officer of the agency:  (a) decides under section 48 not to investigate the disclosure, or not to investigate the disclosure further; and  (b) does not decide to investigate the disclosure under a separate investigative power (as mentioned in section 49); and  (c) is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the conduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under another law or power (other than a separate investigative power). Referral of conduct  (2) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct disclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the other law or power."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c65ce49838f8619f721b1f378e4225ed79a3365effea5310d2b4025f910f208a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "73"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50aa-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50aa-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.73" .
doc:sec-50aa a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "50AA Decision not to investigate—referral for investigation under" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "another law or power Scope  (1) This section applies if the principal officer of the agency:  (a) decides under section 48 not to investigate the disclosure, or not to investigate the disclosure further; and  (b) does not decide to investigate the disclosure under a separate investigative power (as mentioned in section 49); and  (c) is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the conduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under another law or power (other than a separate investigative power). Referral of conduct  (2) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct disclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the other law or power." ;
    cof:pageNumber "73"^^xsd:integer .

