    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if the principal officer of the agency:  (a) decides under section 48 not to investigate the disclosure, or not to investigate the disclosure further; and  (b) does not decide to investigate the disclosure under a separate investigative power (as mentioned in section 49); and  (c) is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the conduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under another law or power (other than a separate investigative power). Referral of conduct" ;
    cof:pageNumber "73"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50aa-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50AA(2) Decision not to investigate—referral for investigation under"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50aa-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct disclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the other law or power." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct disclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the other law or power."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2a253c90f5994328deb95d88c68b960ac2572f5cfeab573826e3154e3066ffde" ;
    values:partOf concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "73"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Principal officer must refer conduct for investigation under other law or power." ;
