    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply:  (a) if the investigator believes on reasonable grounds that the agency to which the investigator belongs has the capacity and the appropriate skills and resources needed:  (i) to investigate the commission of the offence; and  (ii) to meet the requirements of the Commonwealth Director of Public Prosecutions in gathering evidence and preparing briefs of evidence in relation to the commission of the offence; or  (b) if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that the relevant information raises a corruption issue (within the meaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) and:  (i) the corruption issue has been referred under that Act to the person or agency mentioned in subsection (4A); or  (ii) that person or agency is already aware of the issue." ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-4a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56(4A) Disclosure to a member of an Australian police force"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-56-ss-4a ;
    values:originalText "(4A) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(b), the person or agency is:  (a) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or  (b) the IGIS, if the corruption issue concerns:  (i) an intelligence agency; or" ;
    skos:definition "(4A) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(b), the person or agency is:  (a) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or  (b) the IGIS, if the corruption issue concerns:  (i) an intelligence agency; or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cd5abdbcc128ba6d0dfe685752ee986558cfd49316d362a7cd858222814fbf09" ;
    values:partOf concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56 ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of corruption issue to a member of an Australian police force" ;
