    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Division: This Division promotes the operation of this Act by imposing additional obligations on principal officers, authorised officers, supervisors and public officials, and by conferring additional functions on the Ombudsman and the IGIS. Note: The way the additional obligations are complied with (or non-compliance with the additional obligations) may be the subject of a complaint to the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976, or (in the case of an intelligence agency, or AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the Australian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s intelligence functions) to the IGIS under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986." ;
    cof:pageNumber "85"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-59 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59 Additional obligations of principal officers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59 ;
    values:originalText "Facilitating public interest disclosures  (1) The principal officer of an agency must take reasonable steps to ensure that:  (a) the number of authorised officers of the agency is sufficient to ensure that they are readily accessible by public officials who belong to the agency; and  (b) public officials who belong to the agency are aware of the identity of each authorised officer of the agency.  (2) The principal officer of an agency must take reasonable steps to encourage and support:  (a) public officials who make, or are considering making, public interest disclosures relating to the agency; and" ;
    skos:definition "Facilitating public interest disclosures  (1) The principal officer of an agency must take reasonable steps to ensure that:  (a) the number of authorised officers of the agency is sufficient to ensure that they are readily accessible by public officials who belong to the agency; and  (b) public officials who belong to the agency are aware of the identity of each authorised officer of the agency.  (2) The principal officer of an agency must take reasonable steps to encourage and support:  (a) public officials who make, or are considering making, public interest disclosures relating to the agency; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c8c5d9b6d4be048636d2cb601f546712a1e05626f0d05f45cf8341d1a2fee51" ;
    cof:pageNumber "85"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-59-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-59-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.85" .
