concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "67 Secrecy—legal practitioners"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-67 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has obtained information in the person’s capacity as the recipient of a legal practitioner disclosure; and   Administrative matters  Part 4 Treatment of information  Division 2  Section 67  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the person:  (i) discloses the information to another person; or  (ii) uses the information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal advice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest disclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made, or proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal practitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or  (b) the information has previously been lawfully published. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has obtained information in the person’s capacity as the recipient of a legal practitioner disclosure; and   Administrative matters  Part 4 Treatment of information  Division 2  Section 67  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the person:  (i) discloses the information to another person; or  (ii) uses the information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal advice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest disclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made, or proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal practitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or  (b) the information has previously been lawfully published. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4d8b056ab2824c54db12c84d76eec321167a8e186d5ff34a9033c663a1cfebad" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.94" .
