doc:sec-68 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "68 Simplified outline" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Division: This Division defines the key concepts of public official, agency, prescribed authority and principal officer. Subdivision A—Public officials" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-69 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69 Public officials"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-69 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) a public official means an individual mentioned in column 1 of an item of the following table; and  (b) the public official belongs to the agency mentioned in column 2 of the item.  Public officials and the agencies to which they belong Item Column 1 Public official Column 2 Agency to which the public official belongs An APS employee in a Department. The Department. A member of staff of an agency other than a Department (including an APS employee in the agency). The agency. A Secretary of a Department. The Department. The principal officer of an agency other than a Department (see section 73). The agency. An individual who constitutes a prescribed authority. The prescribed authority. A member of a prescribed authority (other than a court). The prescribed authority.   Administrative matters  Part 4 Officials and agencies  Division 3  Section 69  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Public officials and the agencies to which they belong Item Column 1 Public official Column 2 Agency to which the public official belongs A director of a Commonwealth company. The Commonwealth company. A member of the Defence Force, or a cadet, officer or instructor in the Australian Defence Force Cadets. The Defence Department. An AFP appointee (within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979). The Australian Federal Police. A Parliamentary Service employee (within the meaning of the Parliamentary Service Act 1999). The Department in which the Parliamentary service employee is employed. An individual who: (a) is employed by the Commonwealth otherwise than as an APS employee; and (b) performs duties for an agency. The agency. A statutory officeholder, other than an individual covered by any of the above items. Whichever of the following agencies is applicable: (a) if the statutory officeholder is a deputy (however described) of the principal officer of an agency—that agency; (b) if the statutory officeholder performs the duties of his or her office as duties of his or her employment as an officer of or under an agency—that agency; (c) otherwise—the agency ascertained in accordance with the PID rules." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) a public official means an individual mentioned in column 1 of an item of the following table; and  (b) the public official belongs to the agency mentioned in column 2 of the item.  Public officials and the agencies to which they belong Item Column 1 Public official Column 2 Agency to which the public official belongs An APS employee in a Department. The Department. A member of staff of an agency other than a Department (including an APS employee in the agency). The agency. A Secretary of a Department. The Department. The principal officer of an agency other than a Department (see section 73). The agency. An individual who constitutes a prescribed authority. The prescribed authority. A member of a prescribed authority (other than a court). The prescribed authority.   Administrative matters  Part 4 Officials and agencies  Division 3  Section 69  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Public officials and the agencies to which they belong Item Column 1 Public official Column 2 Agency to which the public official belongs A director of a Commonwealth company. The Commonwealth company. A member of the Defence Force, or a cadet, officer or instructor in the Australian Defence Force Cadets. The Defence Department. An AFP appointee (within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979). The Australian Federal Police. A Parliamentary Service employee (within the meaning of the Parliamentary Service Act 1999). The Department in which the Parliamentary service employee is employed. An individual who: (a) is employed by the Commonwealth otherwise than as an APS employee; and (b) performs duties for an agency. The agency. A statutory officeholder, other than an individual covered by any of the above items. Whichever of the following agencies is applicable: (a) if the statutory officeholder is a deputy (however described) of the principal officer of an agency—that agency; (b) if the statutory officeholder"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41ae972dec3b64c1e8d046735de82894b5c55d4994680602a749521b2cc53b70" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines public official for the purposes of the Act." ;
