doc:sec-73b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "73B Machinery of government changes—conduct relating to" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "affected agency  Despite section 35 (which defines when conduct relates to an agency), conduct that occurred before the change time and that would, apart from this section, relate to the affected agency is instead taken, for the purposes of this Act, to relate to the new agency if:  (a) the conduct relates to a transferred function; or  (b) the PID rules provide that conduct of that kind is to be taken to relate to the new agency." ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73C Machinery of government changes—disclosures made before"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-73c ;
    values:originalText "change  (1) This section applies if:  (a) before the change time, a person disclosed information to an authorised officer of an affected agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the affected agency; and  (b) the information concerns conduct that is taken to relate to the new agency under section 73B; and  (c) immediately before the change time, consideration of the disclosure under this Act had not started, or (if it had started) had not ended.  (2) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) the disclosure is taken to have been made to an authorised officer of the new agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the new agency; and  (b) if the disclosure had, before the change time, been allocated to the affected agency, after that time it is taken to have been allocated to the new agency; and  (c) if an investigation under this Act had, before the change time, started in relation to the disclosure, the investigation may continue as if the disclosure had been made in relation to conduct that relates to the new agency; and" ;
    skos:definition "change  (1) This section applies if:  (a) before the change time, a person disclosed information to an authorised officer of an affected agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the affected agency; and  (b) the information concerns conduct that is taken to relate to the new agency under section 73B; and  (c) immediately before the change time, consideration of the disclosure under this Act had not started, or (if it had started) had not ended.  (2) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) the disclosure is taken to have been made to an authorised officer of the new agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the new agency; and  (b) if the disclosure had, before the change time, been allocated to the affected agency, after that time it is taken to have been allocated to the new agency; and  (c) if an investigation under this Act had, before the change time, started in relation to the disclosure, the investigation may continue as if the disclosure had been made in relation to conduct that relates to the new agency; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "12ea12eace7d655f471ce55e34f89b1b77a3d9d05a445ca82877dd2235beaa51" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73c-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.105" .
doc:sec-73c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "73C Machinery of government changes—disclosures made before" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "change  (1) This section applies if:  (a) before the change time, a person disclosed information to an authorised officer of an affected agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the affected agency; and  (b) the information concerns conduct that is taken to relate to the new agency under section 73B; and  (c) immediately before the change time, consideration of the disclosure under this Act had not started, or (if it had started) had not ended.  (2) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) the disclosure is taken to have been made to an authorised officer of the new agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the new agency; and  (b) if the disclosure had, before the change time, been allocated to the affected agency, after that time it is taken to have been allocated to the new agency; and  (c) if an investigation under this Act had, before the change time, started in relation to the disclosure, the investigation may continue as if the disclosure had been made in relation to conduct that relates to the new agency; and" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer .

