doc:sec-73c-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "73C(2) Machinery of government changes—disclosures made before" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this Act:  (a) the disclosure is taken to have been made to an authorised officer of the new agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the new agency; and  (b) if the disclosure had, before the change time, been allocated to the affected agency, after that time it is taken to have been allocated to the new agency; and  (c) if an investigation under this Act had, before the change time, started in relation to the disclosure, the investigation may continue as if the disclosure had been made in relation to conduct that relates to the new agency; and" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73D Machinery of government changes—information transfer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-73d ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) before the change time, a person disclosed information to an authorised officer of an affected agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the affected agency; and  (b) the information concerns conduct that is taken to relate to the new agency under section 73B; and  (c) either:  (i) immediately before the change time, consideration of the disclosure under this Act had not started, or (if it had started) had not ended; or  (ii) before or after the change time, a report into an investigation under section 51 in relation to the disclosure is completed by the principal officer of the affected agency.  (2) The principal officer of the affected agency is authorised to provide the following information (including documents) in relation to the disclosure to the principal officer of the new agency:  (a) any report of the investigation under section 51;  (b) any notice of recommendations by the Ombudsman or the IGIS under section 55;  (c) any other information in relation to the disclosure.   Miscellaneous  Part 5  Section 74  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) before the change time, a person disclosed information to an authorised officer of an affected agency, or to a supervisor belonging to the affected agency; and  (b) the information concerns conduct that is taken to relate to the new agency under section 73B; and  (c) either:  (i) immediately before the change time, consideration of the disclosure under this Act had not started, or (if it had started) had not ended; or  (ii) before or after the change time, a report into an investigation under section 51 in relation to the disclosure is completed by the principal officer of the affected agency.  (2) The principal officer of the affected agency is authorised to provide the following information (including documents) in relation to the disclosure to the principal officer of the new agency:  (a) any report of the investigation under section 51;  (b) any notice of recommendations by the Ombudsman or the IGIS under section 55;  (c) any other information in relation to the disclosure.   Miscellaneous  Part 5  Section 74  Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cb20dc9dc475cea277a4b7a5c791d5631f8e2fb5bf61097b8268564b2982b5c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "106"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73d-ss-1 ;
